{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 complete — fix pushed to Gerrit (NOT submitted/closed; orchestrator lands it)\n\n**Gerrit change: [2463](https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2463)** — commit `80777cb` (`rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO sign-off + Change-Id `Idbc8dc1`). Awaiting `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1`.\n\n### Proven root causes (two independent, per parsimony)\n**RC#1 — Windows collection blackout (defect).** `fcntl` is POSIX-only. Four modules did an *unconditional* module-top `import fcntl`: `_store/lock.py`, `_store/git_locking.py`, `reducer/marker.py`, `_commands/doctor_locks.py`. `import rebar` transitively reaches `doctor_locks.py`, so the ENTIRE package failed to collect off POSIX → `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fcntl'` on the sweep-windows tier. Runtime-proven via `sys.modules['fcntl']=None` (simulated absent module). The codebase already establishes the guard invariant in **three** legitimate shapes — module-top `try/except ImportError→None` (janitor/repo_snapshot/git_fetch), an `if sys.platform != \"win32\"` conditional (`alert_store.py`), and function-local lazy imports (`recent_creates.py`, `hlc.py`). Fix = guard the four with the try/except shape (collectability only; Windows *locking* out of scope — not a declared support target; on non-POSIX `fcntl=None` so a lock call would `AttributeError`, which is acceptable). POSIX unchanged.\n\n**RC#2 — py3.14 network-forbidden (defect); reporter's \"unmocked network call\" was a misdiagnosis.** The autouse `_network_guard` (`tests/conftest.py`) patched `socket.socket.connect` for ALL address families. Python 3.14 changed the Linux default multiprocessing start method `fork`→`forkserver`; forkserver reaches its server over an **AF_UNIX** socket (local IPC, never network), which the all-families guard rejected → the exact `RuntimeError: Network access is forbidden`. Discriminating experiment (forced start methods): fork/spawn=OK, forkserver=BLOCKED. Fix = narrow the `connect` seam to AF_INET/AF_INET6 only, delegating other families to the captured real connect; the `create_connection` seam (real-TCP-only) is unchanged.\n\n### RED→GREEN (held out, mutation-checked)\n- `tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py` — 4 modules + `import rebar` import under a simulated fcntl-less interpreter (subprocess); + AST-gate discrimination (true-positive, a true-negative for each of the three guarded shapes, sanction). Mutation: unwrapping `doctor_locks` → exact `ModuleNotFoundError: import of fcntl halted` RED; restored.\n- `tests/unit/test_network_guard_local_ipc.py` — AF_UNIX connect + a forkserver `Process` start under the guard (GREEN), real AF_INET connect still blocked (teeth). Mutation: reverting the guard to all-families → both RED with the guard RuntimeError; restored.\n- **Original-report replication:** `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py::test_a_contended_fcntl_leg_reads_as_held` under forced `forkserver` → RED (exact ticket error) pre-fix, GREEN post-fix.\n\n### Structural guard (class earns a gate)\n`scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py` — stdlib-only AST scan over `src/rebar`, flags an *unconditional* module-top `import fcntl`, credits try/except **and** `if` (platform) guards **and** function-local imports, with a `# fcntl-guard-ok:` sanction. Wired into `make lint`. Portable: no CI provider required (project.portability). Two `import fcntl` test siblings (`test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py`, `test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py`) now `pytest.importorskip(\"fcntl\")`.\n\n### Validation\n`make lint` ✅, `make typecheck` ✅ (720 files). Parity sweep over the change blast radius (`-k network/socket/fcntl/lock/marker/multiprocess/forkserver/guard/…` across `tests/unit`): **1614 passed, 7 skipped, 0 failed**. Plan-review gate: **certified** (PASS after description corrections).\n\n### Attribution / recommended close\n`caused_by` → **13ad-4c6f-4074-4f43** (commit `7024c35`, \"ci: extend periodic sweep with breadth coverage\") added BOTH the py3.14 must-pass cell and the Windows tier without the portability work. Recommended close: **`--class=plan_defect --caused-by=13ad-4c6f-4074-4f43`**.\n\n### For the orchestrator\nNo design/behavior escalation needed. Implemented directly (fix is mechanism-dictated/mechanical) while preserving strict RED→GREEN + per-defect mutation check + refactor-litmus. **Do not close until change 2463 is `Verified +1`** (green CI is not substitutable by the completion-verifier)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788157450549870217,"uuid":"cd1b39d1-d1b6-4b37-a9ce-27d282c1c692"}